  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_autoencoder(x: list, W_enc: list, b_enc: list, W_dec: list, b_dec: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Autoencoder Forward Pass** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef dl_autoencoder(x: list, W_enc: list, b_enc: list, W_dec: list, b_dec: list) -> dict:\n    X, We, be = np.array(x, dtype=np.float64), np.array(W_enc, dtype=np.float64), np.array(b_enc, dtype=np.float64)\n    Wd, bd = np.array(W_dec, dtype=np.float64), np.array(b_dec, dtype=np.float64)\n    z = np.maximum(0.0, np.dot(X, We) + be)\n    recon = np.dot(z, Wd) + bd\n    return {'latent': np.round(z, 6).tolist(), 'reconstruction': np.round(recon, 6).tolist(), 'mse_loss': round(float(np.mean((X - recon) ** 2)), 6)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
